# `public/data/hackathons.json` and `public/sitemap.xml` are generated by
# `npm run refresh` and rewritten in full each time, so any pull where CI
# refreshed the dataset *and* you refreshed it locally conflicts on the entire
# file. `merge=generated` resolves that by keeping whichever side was scraped
# later — see scripts/merge-generated.mjs.
#
# The driver lives in git config, which can't be committed, so run this once
# per clone to enable it:  npm run setup:merge-driver
# Without it git ignores the attribute and you get a normal conflict.
#
# `-diff` on the dataset: it's one 480KB line of minified JSON, so its textual
# diff is noise in every log and review. Drop that flag if you ever want it back.
public/data/hackathons.json  merge=generated -diff
public/sitemap.xml           merge=generated

# Keep the OG card byte-identical across platforms.
public/og.png  binary
